<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KOCOPIA buys 105,000 tonnes of U.S. corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KOCOPIA buys 105,000 tonnes of U.S. corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Corn Processing Industry Association (KOCOPIA) bought 105,000 tonnes of U.S. yellow No.2 corn from Cargill at $139.60 a tonne C&amp;F, traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Traders said the purchase was made through a private negotiation. The seller has an option to choose the corn shipment from between the Pacific Northwest and the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p> POSITION  TONNE			SHIPMENT</p>
<p>   one    52,500     Aug 10-30 (PNW)  Jul 25-Aug 15 (Gulf)</p>
<p>   two    52,500     Aug 25-Sep 15 (PNW)  Aug 10-30 (Gulf)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
